{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"engineVoicedStubLines","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ours","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV11StubRepliesV","text":"StubReplies","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The game’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"text.stubs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"ours"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The property names still identical to the engine’s wording.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A game that gives itself a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stub floor"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.stubs"},{"text":", rather than an","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"action(…)"},{"type":"text","text":" row per verb — is claiming all ~47 of them, and the claim is easy"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to half-keep: one line left unassigned means a plain modern narrator takes"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over on the turn after a re-voiced one, which is exactly the defect the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dungeon and Zork 1 floors were written to close. Naming each verb in a test","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"catches that; it does not catch a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"forty-eighth","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" stub arriving in the engine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tomorrow, which would slip past every named assertion at once."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So this reads the properties off "},{"code":"GameText.StubReplies","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than listing them: every line the engine actually ships is compared,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and one added tomorrow is compared the day it lands. A property whose type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this cannot render is reported as its own issue rather than skipped, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what keeps “reflected” from quietly meaning “unchecked”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That last sentence has no exception to it as of #246. ","type":"text"},{"code":"give","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" used to be one:","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the one line about two objects, so not a "},{"code":"GameText.Line","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so unreachable by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection and compared by hand below the loop — the single line in here that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"could change shape without the sweep noticing. It takes a "},{"code":"GameText.Gift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"now, and goes through the same door as the other forty-eight.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which sentences each line prints is the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"subject’s"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" business as of #255:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LineSubject.samples(one:many:)"},{"type":"text","text":" supplies them, so a subject arriving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tomorrow is swept the day it lands rather than after somebody teaches a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch here about it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is split out from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the sweep can be tested for being "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"alive"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": a reflection loop that matches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing passes silently, where one asserted to see all forty-nine lines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Asserting","title":"Asserting"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/enginevoiceds